  "question": {
    "text": "The greatest value of <math><mi>c</mi><mo>&#8712;</mo><mi>R</mi></math> for which the system of linear equations&nbsp;<math><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>c</mi><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>c</mi><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>,&nbsp;<math><mi>c</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>c</mi><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>,&nbsp;<math><mi>c</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>c</mi><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>&nbsp;has a non-trivial solution, is"
  },
  "options": [
